.TH SWAYDESK-DOCK 1 2026-11-14 "swaydesk 0.2.1" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-dock \- dock for Sway
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-dock
.br
.B swaydesk\-dock
reload
.br
.B swaydesk\-dock
pin ID
.br
.B swaydesk\-dock
unpin ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
The bottom dock: the pinned applications and the open windows, one dock per session. A second start exits. sway\-theme, the app grid and the pin command find it by its process name.
.PP
The session runs it under the name sway\-dock (a link in the package's helper directory to /usr/bin/swaydesk\-dock); the process name is sway\-dock too.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B reload
Ask the running dock to read its configuration again.
.TP
.B pin ID, unpin ID
Ask the running dock to pin or unpin an application, by the ID of its .desktop file; the app grid uses it. Without a running dock, exit 1 and change nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 0 at once without doing anything: the Python launchers use it to check that the binary and its libraries load.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sway\-dock/config.toml
The dock configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/swaydesk/config.toml
The desktop configuration: language, accent color, GTK and icon themes, folder color, file manager, weather location and holidays.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sway (5),
.BR swaydesk (7),
.BR swaydesk\-drawer (1)
